  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 230 PM EDT Wed Sep 9 2026\n\n- Showers and Storms End This Afternoon/Evening\n\nRadar shows ongoing showers shifting to the south/east ahead of a \ncold front expected to pass in the coming hours. The passage of this \nfront will cause showers and storms to come to an end. HREF mean \nSBCAPE shows a few hundred joules through the afternoon which \nsupports isolated thunderstorm potential until precipitation clears \nthe area.\n\n- Low Chance Of Weekend Rain\n\nOur next chance of precipitation arrives over the weekend as a cold \nfront and weak shortwave cross the area. Weak moisture return is \nexpected to keep much of the weekend dry and PoPs low. For those \nthat see precipitation, amounts should be less than 0.10\".\n\n- Additional showers and storms Monday/Tuesday\n\nA stronger system takes aim at the region Monday as the upper-level \njet moves south into the region. A deepening low associated with \nthis will lead to potentially breezy conditions as well as the \nchance for showers and storms. NBM probabilities suggest a 30-40% \nchance of over 1\" of rainfall, highest across the northwest CWA, so \nwill need to monitor for potential heavy rainfall. Given a modeled \nample LLJ in place, even with questions on available instability, \nwe'll have to monitor potential for storm development.",
